===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|de|goh|sūgan||to suck}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*sūganą}}, from {{der|de|ine-pro|*seuḱ-}}. Compare {{cog|nds|sugen}}, {{cog|nl|zuigen}}, {{cog|da|suge}}.

====Verb====
{{de-verb|saugen<sog,gesogen,söge>}}

# {{lb|de|intransitive}} to [[suck]]; to create under pressure with a tube-like object such as one's mouth
#: {{uxi|de|an etwas '''saugen'''|t=to suck on something}}
# {{lb|de|transitive}} to [[suck]] (something)
# {{lb|de|colloquial|transitive}} to [[download]] something

